{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lfv1eyic","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 1 Offline","year":2008,"examDate":2008,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"basics-of-organic-chemistry","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","topic":"isomerism","type":"mcqm","marks":4,"negMarks":2,"permalink":"pthe-correct-statements-concerning-the-structures-e-f-a-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-feypv5tefzgqxzmt","content":"<p>The correct statement(s) concerning the structures E, F and G is(are) :</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lg94vmxn/28af962c-06cc-4ec2-a826-fd939f61eacc/362e7ab0-d6af-11ed-89f6-65b3651d9edd/file-1lg94vmxo.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1lg94vmxn/28af962c-06cc-4ec2-a826-fd939f61eacc/362e7ab0-d6af-11ed-89f6-65b3651d9edd/file-1lg94vmxo.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 8 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1lg94vmxn/28af962c-06cc-4ec2-a826-fd939f61eacc/362e7ab0-d6af-11ed-89f6-65b3651d9edd/file-1lg94vmxo.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1lg94vmxn/28af962c-06cc-4ec2-a826-fd939f61eacc/362e7ab0-d6af-11ed-89f6-65b3651d9edd/file-1lg94vmxo.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lg94vmxn/28af962c-06cc-4ec2-a826-fd939f61eacc/362e7ab0-d6af-11ed-89f6-65b3651d9edd/file-1lg94vmxo.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1lg94vmxn/28af962c-06cc-4ec2-a826-fd939f61eacc/362e7ab0-d6af-11ed-89f6-65b3651d9edd/file-1lg94vmxo.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1lg94vmxn/28af962c-06cc-4ec2-a826-fd939f61eacc/362e7ab0-d6af-11ed-89f6-65b3651d9edd/file-1lg94vmxo.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1lg94vmxn/28af962c-06cc-4ec2-a826-fd939f61eacc/362e7ab0-d6af-11ed-89f6-65b3651d9edd/file-1lg94vmxo.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"E, F and G are resonance structures."},{"identifier":"B","content":"E, F and E, G are tautomers."},{"identifier":"C","content":"F and G are geometrical isomers."},{"identifier":"D","content":"F and G are diasteromers."}],"correct_options":["B","C","D"],"explanation":"<p>The correct statements concerning the structures E, F and G are:</p>\n<p>(B) E, F and G are tautomers.</p>\n<p>E is in keto form (C=O) and F and G are in enol form (C=C<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>OH)</p>\n<p>(C) F and G are geometrical isomers. F is Z isomer and E is E isomer.</p>\n<p>(D) F and G are diastereomers. They are not mirror images of each other and non-superimposable.</p>"}]}